  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nLegacy DM permission uses mutual follows/admin status and is checked separately from inserting a message. New blocks can therefore be bypassed by old writers. Add a trigger to the existing message table that locks current account authority and requires bilateral canonical consent, participant identity and no block/closure when social policy applies. Pausing the UI/runtime retains restrictions; activation memory cannot be cleared by ordinary updates or deletion.\n\nDepends on **#382** and its stack. **Incomplete cutover; do not activate.** Legacy thread/history readers, full HTTP error mapping and other privacy surfaces still need integration. No new message store, consent backfill or client contract change. Existing legacy behavior is preserved before activation when there is no canonical pair or closure.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- TLA+/TLC: **101 distinct states**, safety and fair progress pass; both unsafe pause and consent variants produce the required authority counterexample.\n- **27 generated INSERT outcomes** from actual checked model observations. The old unguarded INSERT fails generated case 2 (closed account); the new trigger passes.\n- Private PostgreSQL: real block-first and send-first lock barriers, participant/lifecycle denials, edit/upsert protection, unsupported isolation rejection, retained activation and preserved-write pause/reapply pass.\n- Complete schema-only baseline + **102 registered migrations**: old message preserved, blocked retry denied after pause; prior feed/graph reconciliation passes on PostgreSQL 16.10.\n- Small server-side fixture benchmark: active INSERT p95 **1.615 ms**, before trigger **0.110 ms**, below the predeclared 10 ms added-p95 limit. Not production/high-degree evidence.\n- **21 workflow/scope tests pass**, catalog audit passes. [Hosted social CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35011873153) and [full CI](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35011873154) both passed at implementation `efc827f7628afe084db173be627d0d7f71d0142a`, including actual PostgreSQL 17 model-derived DM/race/schema checks and backend runtime verification. Later evidence-only revisions are separate.\n\nSee `docs/social/dm-write-boundary.md` for exact commands, model bounds, traceability, evidence and limitations. The model abstracts an atomic INSERT boundary; concrete locking is qualified by database races, not a proof of every lock graph.\n\n## Migration, flags and rollback\n\nApply additive `2026-09-15_social_v2_dm_write_boundary.sql` after foundation/read models and existing chat schema. Not registered for automatic production boot. Single-row activation backfill and trigger/function replacement are transactional/idempotent. READ COMMITTED is required explicitly to prevent stale transaction snapshots from bypassing a first block.\n\nProduction flags remain inactive. Pause preserves messages, consent/block tombstones, command history and activation memory. Keep the write guard during application rollback; removing it would restore the demonstrated bypass. Old readers remain unsafe for full privacy. No destructive down migration or claim of full old/new application coexistence.\n\nDraft and unmerged; no deployment command. Branch-scoped Vercel suppression and `[CF-Pages-Skip]` retained. Earlier automatic deployment exceptions remain unresolved and documented.\n\n\n## Parent reconciliation \u2014 2026-09-16\n\nNormal merge `e03ce193c2e9c6788fad5f1360aef1088006616f` preserves original head `50131ef4489e980846a7d524f27475828aeef7cd` and current parent `2be39150f626dcd5181951532a8ebe25a3ce3fa4`. No shared history was rewritten. Social runtime, SQL, models, tests and social workflow remain byte-identical to the original head. Previously merged artwork and Instagram changes from the parent remain intact; catalog outputs were regenerated with the unchanged strict policy.\n\nVerified locally on the reconciled runtime tree: DM consent/lifecycle and pause write-denial assertions, both real block/send race orders, complete PostgreSQL schema and registered migrations, additive reapply and data preservation, positive DM model and two expected unsafe counterexamples, 21 CI workflow/scope tests, and strict catalog JSON and CSV. All commands exited 0. The isolated runtime-tested tree and publish tree differ only in regenerated catalog reports.\n\nNew exact-head hosted checks and any renewed review remain required. Existing feature and migration activation gates are unchanged. No manual deployment was performed. Native-stack integration remains separately blocked by its linear-history requirement; this update does not claim the stack is merged.\n",
